              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97031",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97031"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-97031?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3E%3D1.27.0-0%2C%3C1.27.2",
              "help": {
                "text": "Multiple ECH outer extension references are not permitted under RFC 9849; previously, a client could send a well-crafted packet that could trigger memory exhaustion in the server process by specifying multiple references.\n\nWe now reject these as malformed and curb the memory amplification vector as a result.\n",
                "markdown": "> Multiple ECH outer extension references are not permitted under RFC 9849; previously, a client could send a well-crafted packet that could trigger memory exhaustion in the server process by specifying multiple references.\n\nWe now reject these as malformed and curb the memory amplification vector as a result.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.27.1  |\n|Affected range  >=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2        |\n|Fixed version   1.27.2                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "1.27.2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.27.1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78663",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78663"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-78663?s=golang&n=net&ns=golang.org%2Fx&t=golang&vr=%3C0.60.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.\n",
                "markdown": "> The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.\n\n|                                                    |\n|Package         pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@0.58.0  |\n|Affected range  <0.60.0                             |\n|Fixed version   0.60.0                              |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
                "fixed_version": "1.27.2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@0.58.0",
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.27.1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "tags": [
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56857",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56857"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56857?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3E%3D1.27.0-0%2C%3C1.27.2",
              "help": {
                "text": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n",
                "markdown": "> On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.27.1  |\n|Affected range  >=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2        |\n|Fixed version   1.27.2                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
                "fixed_version": "1.27.2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.27.1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8",
                "tags": [
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "1.21.0"
        }
